I'm concluding on a single root cause: `search`, with an HTTP-layer slowdown on its calls to `rate`. No restarts or network error counters changed, and no per-connection network metrics exist in this case.

```json
{
  "root_causes": [
    {
      "service": "search",
      "fault_kind": "http_slow",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "kind": "trace",
          "sql": "SELECT c.service_name caller, s.service_name callee, count(*) n, round(quantile_cont(c.duration,0.5)/1e6,1) client_p50_ms, round(quantile_cont(s.duration,0.5)/1e6,2) server_p50_ms, round(quantile_cont(c.duration-s.duration,0.5)/1e6,1) overhead_p50_ms, round(min(c.duration-s.duration)/1e6,1) overhead_min_ms, round(max(c.duration-s.duration)/1e6,1) overhead_max_ms FROM abnormal_traces c JOIN abnormal_traces s ON s.parent_span_id=c.span_id AND s.trace_id=c.trace_id WHERE c.attr_span_kind='Client' AND s.attr_span_kind='Server' GROUP BY 1,2 ORDER BY 1,2",
          "claim": "search→rate client calls add about 1537 ms overhead (min 1351 ms) while rate's server span takes about 0.7 ms; other edges add about 0.3 ms."
        },
        {
          "kind": "trace",
          "sql": "WITH slow AS (SELECT trace_id FROM abnormal_traces WHERE span_name='search.Search/Nearby' AND service_name='search' ORDER BY duration DESC LIMIT 1) SELECT t.service_name, t.span_name, t.attr_span_kind, round(t.duration/1e6,1) ms FROM abnormal_traces t JOIN slow USING(trace_id) ORDER BY t.time",
          "claim": "In the slowest trace, search's rate.Rate/GetRates client span lasts about 3023 ms while rate's server span lasts 0.8 ms."
        },
        {
          "kind": "trace",
          "sql": "SELECT service_name, span_name, count(*) n, round(quantile_cont(duration,0.95)/1e6,1) p95_ms FROM abnormal_traces WHERE service_name='rate' AND span_name='rate.Rate/GetRates' GROUP BY 1,2",
          "claim": "rate's own GetRates server spans stay around 1 ms p95 during the incident, so rate itself is not slow."
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "propagation": [
    {
      "from": "search",
      "to": "frontend",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "kind": "trace",
          "sql": "SELECT c.service_name caller, s.service_name callee, count(*) n, round(quantile_cont(c.duration,0.5)/1e6,1) client_p50_ms, round(quantile_cont(s.duration,0.5)/1e6,1) server_p50_ms, round(quantile_cont(c.duration-s.duration,0.5)/1e6,1) overhead_p50_ms FROM abnormal_traces c JOIN abnormal_traces s ON s.parent_span_id=c.span_id AND s.trace_id=c.trace_id WHERE c.attr_span_kind='Client' AND s.attr_span_kind='Server' AND c.service_name='frontend' AND s.service_name='search' GROUP BY 1,2",
          "claim": "frontend's client span to search carries the full ~1538 ms, with only ~0.3 ms overhead, so search's delay flows straight into frontend's HTTP /hotels."
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
```

